From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 13:08:34 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] compaction: terminal/execute_code stubs count
 decoded lines, keep edges, say output was elided; image miss lists siblings

A hub session compacted a 16-path figure listing to '[terminal] ran ... -> exit 0, 1 lines output'
(newlines counted in the JSON-escaped result, no path kept), then asked vision_analyze for four
invented figure names. Now: line counts come from the decoded output field; the stub keeps the first
and last line and ends '(output elided: re-run or list the dir to see it)'; short listings (<=12 lines,
<=600 chars) stay verbatim through the ordinary prune pass; a local-backend media miss names up to 10
real sibling files sharing the stem prefix. Self-heal defect agent-6b77b9f55a.
